":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"```json\n{\"blind_id\":\"C025\",\"coverage\":[{\"point\":1,\"credit\":1,\"reason\":\"Says appointing a principal underwriter 'does not guarantee sales or asset gathering' and that 'the underwriter alone does not determine distribution outcomes.'\"},{\"point\":2,\"credit\":1,\"reason\":\"Separates the legal/operational distributor role from 'separately contracted marketing' (sales force, wholesaling, advertising) and from intermediary access (wirehouse/RIA/model approvals), and notes that platform packages vary.\"}],\"central_error\":null,\"local_error\":null,\"grade\":\"correct\",\"rationale\":\"Both required minimums are fully covered. The answer explicitly rejects the central error. Its description of the distributor's operational role (creation/redemption order processing, AP coordination) is broadly consistent with ETF distributor arrangements, so it is not a material falsehood. It does not claim that every sponsor must employ its own sales team. Not citing the Simplify/Foreside example is an omission and does not reduce the grade.\"}\n```","ttft_ms":3045,"type":"result","duration_ms":5841,"uuid":"71fa03d0-53f5-48b9-a50c-609c126a39fc","ttft_stream_ms":1522,"time_to_request_ms":67,"first_content_frame_ms":1522,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
